Cell[TextData[{
 "The dashed black curve is an independently-defined exponential, plotted on \
top of, not derived from, the alpha=1 Gamma curve.\nAt the other end, \
alpha=0.3 is ",
 StyleBox["not",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " a wide, spread-out bump : it diverges toward infinity right at \[Sigma]=0 \
(the Gamma density behaves like ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["\[Sigma]", 
   RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "-", "1"}]]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a850a741-b91c-4255-8aeb-53bdb9f40442"],
 " near the origin, which blows up whenever \[Alpha]<1) and then decreases \
monotonically -- more concentrated at zero than the exponential itself, not \
less, with a correspondingly heavier tail out at large \[Sigma] to keep the \
total probability equal to one. Large \[Alpha] collapses the distribution \
toward a narrow spike at the mean instead -- exactly the \[Alpha]\[Rule]\
\[Infinity] limit where the randomized rate stops being random at all and the \
whole family reduces back to plain classical transport."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.999241269970932*^9, 
  3.999241282682239*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e9825944-11b4-451f-8ea3-\
f11f42336127"],

Cell["\<\
And the crossing point itself, directly: CV as a function of alpha.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"77431389-d2d7-4f38-8f97-3daafd809ba3"],

